<GuideLayout
  title="Provide layers"
  description="The CMS service is pluggable. Provide one layer per dependency — or use the convenience layers bundled with the library."
  nextGuide={{ href: "/guides/building-a-site/", label: "Build a content site" }}
>
  <p>
    Effect layers are the wiring diagram. Nearly Headless CMS expects you to provide persistence,
    authorization, identity, and identifier generation. The library composes them into
    <code>Cms.Service</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>One file per layer in the Example CMS</h2>
  <p>The reference app splits dependencies into a <code>layers/</code> folder:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>layers/authorization.ts</code> — who can do what</li>
    <li><code>layers/identity.ts</code> — who is making this request</li>
    <li><code>layers/identifiers.ts</code> — how new IDs are generated</li>
    <li><code>layers/persistence.ts</code> — where entries and assets are stored</li>
    <li><code>layers/cms.ts</code> — merges everything into <code>Cms.makeLayer</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Want filesystem storage with development defaults already wired? Import the convenience layer:</p>
  <pre><code>{`import { Filesystem } from "nearly-headless-cms/layers"

const cmsLayer = Filesystem.cms({
  root: ".data/my-cms/persistence",
  definitionSnapshot: snapshot,
  operationContracts: [...deliveryOps, ...managementOps],
})`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Replace any layer without forking the library</h2>
  <p>
    Convenience layers are optional. You can import <code>Cms.makeLayer</code> directly and provide
    your own <code>Persistence.EntryPersistence</code> implementation, or build a layer from the
    service definition using Effect's layer utilities.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`import { Cms } from "nearly-headless-cms"
import { Layer } from "effect"
import { layer as authorizationLayer } from "./layers/authorization.ts"
import { layer as identityLayer } from "./layers/identity.ts"
import { layer as persistenceLayer } from "./layers/persistence.ts"

const cmsLayer = Cms.makeLayer({ operationContracts })
  .pipe(Layer.provide(Layer.mergeAll(
    authorizationLayer,
    identityLayer,
    persistenceLayer,
  )))`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Development vs production</h2>
  <p>
    Use <code>InMemory.cms</code> for tests and prototypes. Use
    <code>Filesystem.cms</code> or your own durable adapter when you need data to survive restarts.
    The CMS service interface stays the same.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
